# Kernel governance seed (trust-kernel/01, decisions 019 and 087).
#
# This file requests reviewers. It does not require them, and under
# decision 087 nothing on the host does either: every pull request here is
# authored under the founder's own account and the host forbids approving
# your own, so a required-approval rule was unsatisfiable by the only human
# in the repository. What the host enforces instead is a ruleset blocking
# force pushes and branch deletion on main, and what enforces kernel review
# is the loop's own gates: clean-context verification, code review, and the
# founder's read at merge.
#
# checks/kernel-governance.mjs asserts the host half by querying the host,
# precisely so the presence of this file is never mistaken for a rule being
# in force. Required approvals return here the day a second maintainer
# holds write access; 087 writes that trigger down.

# The frozen core: canonicalization, sign/verify, chain append/verify, and
# tree construction and proofs. Everything a subtle bug here would be
# unrecoverable in.
